{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:32e58a32aeabac70","name":"Silooth","source":{"id":"source:reference-32e58a32aeabac70","title":"Silooth","revision":20529,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:01:43Z","sha256":"b7fcb64e966ae76d3df66350fc60c2964c9ddb021c09b8af894b6794534d0583","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20529","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Silooth&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-32e58a32aeabac70","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Silooths were once docile swamp creatures no larger than ",{"tag":"a","children":["Womp Rats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Womp_Rats"},". Sith experiments on these creatures made them grow as large as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Banthas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Banthas"}," and thickened their carapaces. These experiments also heightened their ferocity. Silooths clack their mandibles loudly; the only time they fall quiet is when their jaws have found something to crush. The only thing that stops a Silooth attack is death- either the victim's or the Silooth's. Silooths have poor ranged vision and are unable to see anything past 12 squares. Nevertheless, they possess acid sacs that allow them to spew acid at enemies within their sight.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," first unleashed these creatures during the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kalsunor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kalsunor?action=edit&redlink=1"}," thousands of years before the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},". The Silooths annihilated everything in their path, ravaging ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kalsunor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kalsunor?action=edit&redlink=1"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," left the planet to the Silooths and never looked back. While the Jedi Archives refer to the planet as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kalsunor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kalsunor?action=edit&redlink=1"},", no planet by that name exists in the Republic's thousands of years of records. The true name and location of the planet may exist somewhere, perhaps in a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Holocron"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Holocron"}," yet to be found. There is an old fringer's tale about a planet overrun with such creatures. Were someone to stumble upon a Silooth colony, capture some live specimens, and introduce them into another ecosystem, the results could be devastating.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Silooth Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Silooths represent an extreme example of Sith Alchemy. They are worthy adversaries for Jedi Knights. Because the existence of the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kalsunor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kalsunor?action=edit&redlink=1"}," has been hidden, adventures could be devoted to discovering this lost world ravaged by creatures ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," themselves could barely control. A crash-landing on the uncharted planet of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kalsunor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kalsunor?action=edit&redlink=1"}," is a terrifying adventure of survival. The heroes would have to fend off the creatures while they repair their ship.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Silooth Statistics (CL 11)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," Limited Vision, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 19 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 19), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 25, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 162, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 5, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 35\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 8 Squares; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Powerful Charge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Powerful_Charge","referenceId":"reference:d7f59c39adb93fd7"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," Bite +19 (2d6+16)\n"]},{"tag":"p",